  "text": "Let's analyze the sequence defined by the given recurrence relation:\n\\[ x_1 = \\frac{25}{11}, \\]\n\\[ x_{k+1} = \\frac{1}{3} \\left( x_k + \\frac{1}{x_k} - 1 \\right). \\]\n\nFirst, let's investigate the behavior of the sequence. We need to find a pattern or a periodicity in the sequence. To do this, we can compute the first few terms of the sequence.\n\n1. Calculate \\( x_2 \\):\n\\[ x_2 = \\frac{1}{3} \\left( \\frac{25}{11} + \\frac{1}{\\frac{25}{11}} - 1 \\right) = \\frac{1}{3} \\left( \\frac{25}{11} + \\frac{11}{25} - 1 \\right). \\]\n\\[ x_2 = \\frac{1}{3} \\left( \\frac{25 \\cdot 25 + 11 \\cdot 11 - 275}{275} \\right) = \\frac{1}{3} \\left( \\frac{625 + 121 - 275}{275} \\right) = \\frac{1}{3} \\left( \\frac{471}{275} \\right) = \\frac{471}{825}. \\]\n\n2. Calculate \\( x_3 \\):\n\\[ x_3 = \\frac{1}{3} \\left( \\frac{471}{825} + \\frac{1}{\\frac{471}{825}} - 1 \\right) = \\frac{1}{3} \\left( \\frac{471}{825} + \\frac{825}{471} - 1 \\right). \\]\n\\[ x_3 = \\frac{1}{3} \\left( \\frac{471 \\cdot 471 + 825 \\cdot 825 - 825 \\cdot 825}{825 \\cdot 471} \\right) = \\frac{1}{3} \\left( \\frac{471^2}{825 \\cdot 471} \\right) = \\frac{1}{3} \\left( \\frac{471}{825} \\right) = \\frac{471}{2475}. \\]\n\n3. Calculate \\( x_4 \\):\n\\[ x_4 = \\frac{1}{3} \\left( \\frac{471}{2475} + \\frac{1}{\\frac{471}{2475}} - 1 \\right) = \\frac{1}{3} \\left( \\frac{471}{2475} + \\frac{2475}{471} - 1 \\right). \\]\n\\[ x_4 = \\frac{1}{3} \\left( \\frac{471 \\cdot 471 + 2475 \\cdot 2475 - 2475 \\cdot 2475}{2475 \\cdot 471} \\right) = \\frac{1}{3} \\left( \\frac{471^2}{2475 \\cdot 471} \\right) = \\frac{1}{3} \\left( \\frac{471}{2475} \\right) = \\frac{471}{7425}. \\]\n\nFrom the calculations, we observe that the sequence \\( x_k \\) seems to be converging to a fixed point. To find this fixed point, we set \\( x_{k+1} = x_k = x \\):\n\\[ x = \\frac{1}{3} \\left( x + \\frac{1}{x} - 1 \\right). \\]\nMultiplying both sides by 3:\n\\[ 3x = x + \\frac{1}{x} - 1. \\]\nRearranging terms:\n\\[ 2x = \\frac{1}{x} - 1. \\]\nMultiplying both sides by \\( x \\):\n\\[ 2x^2 = 1 - x. \\]\nRearranging terms:\n\\[ 2x^2 + x - 1 = 0. \\]\nThis is a quadratic equation. Solving for \\( x \\) using the quadratic formula \\( x = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a} \\):\n\\[ x = \\frac{-1 \\pm \\sqrt{1 + 8}}{4} = \\frac{-1 \\pm 3}{4}. \\]\nSo, the solutions are:\n\\[ x = \\frac{1}{2} \\quad \\text{or} \\quad x = -1. \\]\nSince \\( x_1 = \\frac{25}{11} > 0 \\), the fixed point must be \\( x = \\frac{1}{2} \\).\n\nGiven that the sequence converges to \\( \\frac{1}{2} \\), we can express \\( x_{2025} \\) as \\( \\frac{1}{2} \\). Therefore, \\( m = 1 \\) and \\( n = 2 \\), and the remainder when \\( m + n \\) is divided by 1000 is:\n\\[ 1 + 2 = 3. \\]\nSo, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{3}\n\\]",
